 {"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-18", "priority": "P2", "status": "complete", "title": "[dogfood:P2] connect-muster.sh hardcodes :8766 (would start a second daemon on a collision host) and health-checks :8767, a port pinned by nothing", "detail": "connect-muster.sh step 1 nohups `off-by-one --db <repo>/off-by-one.db` when :8766 is not healthy \u2014 on a host where a foreign daemon owns 8766 (the README's own documented collision scenario) a real run would bind-fail at best and, with a different -db default, risk a second writer against shared state. Step 4 then health-checks http://localhost:8767/health, a port nothing in muster-config.yaml (transport: stdio) or any config pins. OFF_BY_ONE_URL overrides the target but is undocumented anywhere in README/docs. Fix direction: derive ports from one config source, honor OFF_BY_ONE_PORT/OFF_BY_ONE_URL consistently, document the env override, and refuse to start a daemon whose health check returns a FOREIGN identity (e.g. check /health then -version) instead of blindly nohuping.", "source": "dogfood tick off-by-one-dogfood-2026-09-24-15-47-25", "created_by": "off-by-one-dogfood", "created_at": "2026-09-24", "acceptance_criteria": "connect-muster.sh --dry-run --check-only on a port-collision host reports the collision and starts nothing; the health-check port comes from config; OFF_BY_ONE_URL/OFF_BY_ONE_PORT overrides documented in README Configuration.", "evidence": "scripts/connect-muster.sh lines ~46-110; dry-run transcript 2026-09-24 (both ports observed); muster-config.yaml transport stdio", "completed_at": "2026-09-25T06:05:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-25T06:05:00Z", "foreman_note": "Worker commit 8b19494 (wt branch, bundled with DF-13 same-file blast radius), wave-merged 3722faa: connect-muster.sh honors OFF_BY_ONE_URL port. Judge OB-DF1318 tier2 PASS (verdict abe42c34)."}
 {"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-19", "priority": "P3", "status": "pending", "title": "[dogfood:P3] MusterFlow table output truncates wide fields to ~120 chars — discover answers and queue entries unreadable without --output json (musterflow-side, DF-038 filed there)", "detail": "Through the generated CLI (`musterflow Off-by-One discovery discover-solution ...`), the default table renders `answer` as a ~120-char truncated JSON string; the full solution is only visible with `--output json` or `-r/--raw`, and nothing in the truncated output hints at those flags. A real consumer discovers this by trial. Filed as DF-038 on the musterflow board (this repo is the affected consumer); reproduced 2026-09-24 against the live lab. Fix belongs to musterflow (ellipsize with a hint, or wrap), mirrored here only as a consumer note.", "source": "dogfood tick off-by-one-dogfood-2026-09-24-15-47-25", "created_by": "off-by-one-dogfood", "created_at": "2026-09-24", "acceptance_criteria": "musterflow default table either wraps long fields or prints a one-line hint naming --output json; off-by-one docs note the flag for consumers.", "evidence": "CLI transcripts in docs/dogfood/2026-09-24-integration.md (truncated 'answer {...' lines); musterflow board DF-038"}
 {"id": "DF-OFF-BY-ONE-20", "priority": "P3", "status": "complete", "title": "[dogfood:P3] q= search token semantics unstated — 'pep 668' (3 hits incl FTS noise) vs 'pep668' (exactly the class) differ; prefix- works, suffix- does not", "detail": "GET /api/v1/problems?q=... tokenizes on whitespace and ANDs the tokens: q='pep 668' returns 3 rows (the exact class plus python-sdk-e2e-battery / board-duckdb-mirror-stale via FTS noise); q='pep668' returns exactly 1. Right-truncation works ('pep66%' style matching within a token), left-truncation does not. Not a bug — but a one-sentence statement of the semantics in docs/api-reference.md would remove the guesswork a consumer hits on their first empty-feeling search.", "source": "dogfood tick off-by-one-dogfood-2026-09-24-15-47-25", "created_by": "off-by-one-dogfood", "created_at": "2026-09-24", "acceptance_criteria": "api-reference.md documents q= tokenization/AND semantics and the truncation direction.", "evidence": "curl transcripts 2026-09-24: q='pep 668' total:3 vs q='pep668' total:1", "completed_at": "2026-09-25T18:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-25T18:50:00Z", "foreman_note": "Foreman-direct ba4d637: docs/api-reference.md GET /api/v1/problems section documents q= as a SINGLE FTS5 phrase (internal/graph/search.go:44) — whole-token adjacent matching, no token-AND, no left truncation, no wildcard. The row's evidence claim ('tokenizes on whitespace and ANDs tokens; prefix works') was DISPROVEN by live probes + code read; criterion satisfied with the true semantics. Judge OB-DF20 PASS 4f27fd49. Post-debug class submitted: sqlite-fts5-phrase-wrapping-changes-multi-token-query-semantics."}
